1
00:00:00,433 --> 00:00:02,705
But she said that she's safe,
and that I shouldn't worry.

2
00:00:02,705 --> 00:00:05,197
She said that she's sorry for worrying us.

3
00:00:05,197 --> 00:00:09,093
And she told me to keep it a secret
from her husband.

4
00:00:13,081 --> 00:00:16,013
<i>This is getting interesting.</i>

5
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:20,873
<i>A Sakiko Seo whom we don't know</i>

6
00:00:20,873 --> 00:00:24,117
<i>might be out there somewhere.</i>

7
00:00:29,261 --> 00:00:30,697
I'm relieved.

8
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,161
What?

9
00:00:32,161 --> 00:00:36,073
Sacchan's safe, right?

10
00:00:36,073 --> 00:00:37,705
Ah, yes.

11
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:41,293
When she contacted you,
did she say anything about her location?

12
00:00:44,705 --> 00:00:46,953
Really?

13
00:00:46,953 --> 00:00:48,313
What about you, Mr. Miyauchi?

14
00:00:48,313 --> 00:00:49,561
Oh, well...

15
00:00:49,561 --> 00:00:52,613
I heard the sound of waves in the background.

16
00:00:52,613 --> 00:00:56,853
So I figured she was probably near the ocean.

17
00:00:56,853 --> 00:00:59,745
Sorry, I didn't mean to tease you.

18
00:00:59,745 --> 00:01:01,661
I think she's alive.

19
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:06,013
I mean, she seems pretty tough, doesn't she?

20
00:01:07,253 --> 00:01:08,973
Okay.

21
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:14,573
Thank you all for gathering here.

22
00:01:14,573 --> 00:01:16,313
Wait, we're done?

23
00:01:16,313 --> 00:01:20,737
Talking more won't help us find her.

24
00:01:20,737 --> 00:01:23,133
I feel like we're even more confused now.

25
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:25,369
If Sacchan does come back...

26
00:01:25,369 --> 00:01:27,777
I think she'll go to your place, Mr. Sonoda.

27
00:01:27,777 --> 00:01:29,125
You're still saying that?

28
00:01:29,125 --> 00:01:32,613
If she does, please take care of her.

29
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:35,973
What?

30
00:01:36,769 --> 00:01:39,073
Chizuru.

31
00:01:39,073 --> 00:01:40,817
Hm?

32
00:01:44,253 --> 00:01:48,901
She gets bored easily, loves new things,
and moves on fast.

33
00:01:48,901 --> 00:01:50,709
What does that mean?

34
00:01:50,709 --> 00:01:53,993
You didn't give any specific examples.

35
00:01:53,993 --> 00:01:56,661
Well, I couldn't really say, of course.

36
00:01:56,661 --> 00:02:01,785
Sakiko really cared about you.

37
00:02:01,785 --> 00:02:04,713
But you were hiding your past.

38
00:02:04,713 --> 00:02:07,373
And now Sakiko has disappeared.

39
00:02:11,257 --> 00:02:13,993
I really don't know where she is.

40
00:02:13,993 --> 00:02:18,093
But I do have an idea
of who she might be with.

41
00:02:18,853 --> 00:02:20,609
Huh?

42
00:02:25,021 --> 00:02:26,973
<i>Chizuru?</i>

43
00:02:26,973 --> 00:02:29,153
- Sacchan!
- You sound well.

44
00:02:29,153 --> 00:02:30,977
Are you eating properly?

45
00:02:30,977 --> 00:02:34,569
<i>Yeah, we're having a barbecue
and I'm eating way too much.</i>

46
00:02:34,569 --> 00:02:36,593
Well, that's good.

47
00:02:36,593 --> 00:02:38,417
If it's a barbecue, you're not alone, right?

48
00:02:38,417 --> 00:02:39,701
Who are you with?

49
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:42,653
<i>What? I'm sure you can guess.</i>

50
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:45,085
Atsuhiko?

51
00:02:45,085 --> 00:02:47,389
<i>That's right!</i>

52
00:02:47,389 --> 00:02:50,181
So you're staying with Atsuhiko?

53
00:02:50,181 --> 00:02:51,705
He's not in Tokyo now, right?

54
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:53,993
<i>Atsu, it's Chizuru.</i>

55
00:02:53,993 --> 00:02:55,749
Sakiko, are you listening?

56
00:02:55,749 --> 00:02:58,833
<i>Chizuru? Long time no see.</i>

57
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:01,233
Long time no see.

58
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:03,369
- <i>There's one here too.</i>
- That looks like fun.

59
00:03:03,369 --> 00:03:06,893
<i>The kids are thrilled that Sakiko's here.</i>

60
00:03:07,849 --> 00:03:10,053
Where do you live now, Atsuhiko?

61
00:03:10,053 --> 00:03:11,429
<i>Oh, I'm in Chiba now.</i>

62
00:03:11,429 --> 00:03:13,085
<i>I'm a fisherman.</i>

63
00:03:13,085 --> 00:03:17,725
Wow! The fish there must be delicious.

64
00:03:17,725 --> 00:03:19,053
Can I come visit too?

65
00:03:19,053 --> 00:03:22,433
- <i>Yeah, please come!</i>
- <i>We'll be waiting!</i>

66
00:03:22,433 --> 00:03:24,517
- <i>Please do come!</i>
- No problem.

67
00:03:24,517 --> 00:03:27,365
Sakiko, can you send me the address
of where you're staying on LINE?

68
00:03:27,365 --> 00:03:29,277
Chiba's a big place.

69
00:03:29,277 --> 00:03:31,705
<i>Oh yes, will do!</i>

70
00:03:31,705 --> 00:03:35,613
- Okay, talk to you later.
- <i>Okay!</i>

71
00:03:40,961 --> 00:03:42,493
That's really strange.

72
00:03:42,493 --> 00:03:46,569
Just a minute ago, I was seriously
worried that she might be dead.

73
00:03:46,569 --> 00:03:49,269
And now I'm shocked that she's so energetic.

74
00:03:49,269 --> 00:03:52,865
Who's that Atsuhiko guy?

75
00:03:52,865 --> 00:03:56,449
You should ask Sakiko about that.

76
00:03:56,449 --> 00:03:59,241
Oh, here it is.

77
00:03:59,241 --> 00:04:01,773
Okay, here's the address.

78
00:04:01,773 --> 00:04:03,597
Chiba.

79
00:04:06,757 --> 00:04:08,549
Thank you.

80
00:04:15,125 --> 00:04:17,253
Just get divorced.

81
00:04:18,237 --> 00:04:24,013
The Sakiko I know would have moved on
the moment he disappeared.

82
00:04:24,877 --> 00:04:28,033
That's the me you know.

83
00:04:28,033 --> 00:04:30,789
- Here you go.
- Yum!

84
00:04:30,789 --> 00:04:33,633
- Hey, eat something other than meat.
- No, I don't want to!

85
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:34,689
- It's not about what you want.
- Okay.

86
00:04:34,689 --> 00:04:36,593
- Come on, eat up.
- Eat up, do your best.

87
00:04:36,593 --> 00:04:38,605
I don't want to.

88
00:04:38,605 --> 00:04:40,717
Sakiko!

89
00:04:40,717 --> 00:04:42,545
- Oh, Kokoa?
- You're late!

90
00:04:42,545 --> 00:04:44,741
- Nice to meet you, thanks for having me.
- They've eaten it all!

91
00:04:44,741 --> 00:04:47,029
Wow, the real Sakiko.

92
00:04:47,029 --> 00:04:49,629
I never thought I'd meet you
in person. It's an honor.

93
00:04:49,629 --> 00:04:51,241
- What are you talking about?
- Thank you, thank you.

94
00:04:51,241 --> 00:04:53,769
- Sit down, sit down.
- Sorry about that.

95
00:04:53,769 --> 00:04:54,783
Thanks for looking after the kids

96
00:04:54,783 --> 00:04:55,997
- while I was out.
- No problem at all.

97
00:04:55,997 --> 00:04:57,849
I had fun playing with them.

98
00:04:57,849 --> 00:04:59,429
Yeah, but still.

99
00:04:59,429 --> 00:05:01,313
Thanks for the clothes.

100
00:05:01,313 --> 00:05:02,581
They look great on you.

101
00:05:02,581 --> 00:05:04,993
Kokoa, want some meat?

102
00:05:04,993 --> 00:05:07,005
Huh? Thanks, Haru.

103
00:05:07,005 --> 00:05:08,653
Call me Mama.

104
00:05:08,653 --> 00:05:10,421
Here's a shell for you, Kokoa.

105
00:05:10,421 --> 00:05:14,273
Huh? Thanks, Himeka. Call me Mama.

106
00:05:15,009 --> 00:05:16,329
They're so cute.

107
00:05:16,329 --> 00:05:18,201
This is nice.

108
00:05:18,201 --> 00:05:20,493
- It's really a family.
- Let's eat!

109
00:05:20,493 --> 00:05:23,501
You have a family in Tokyo, you know.

110
00:05:23,501 --> 00:05:26,373
If you're not divorced yet,
then that's your family.

111
00:05:29,477 --> 00:05:32,301
Oh, what do you want to drink?

112
00:05:32,301 --> 00:05:35,673
[Hanahama]

113
00:05:51,057 --> 00:05:55,869
[Episode 9]

114
00:06:06,385 --> 00:06:09,553
Are you Sakiko's husband?

115
00:06:09,553 --> 00:06:11,005
Sorry for the trouble.
Thank you for everything.

116
00:06:11,005 --> 00:06:13,673
- Where's Sacchan?
- Huh.

117
00:06:13,673 --> 00:06:15,425
So this is how it is. I see.

118
00:06:15,425 --> 00:06:17,273
Well, where's Sacchan?

119
00:06:17,273 --> 00:06:19,417
What now? Will you stay the night?

120
00:06:19,417 --> 00:06:22,193
No, I'm here to take Sacchan home.

121
00:06:22,193 --> 00:06:25,737
Sakiko went back to Tokyo.

122
00:06:25,737 --> 00:06:27,537
What?

123
00:06:30,913 --> 00:06:33,941
Sorry for the trouble.

124
00:06:33,941 --> 00:06:36,292
You caused quite a stir.

125
00:06:36,292 --> 00:06:39,345
Anyway, you don't need to report to me.

126
00:06:39,345 --> 00:06:40,349
Just send me a message on LINE.

127
00:06:40,349 --> 00:06:43,933
Have you talked to Mitsuru yet?

128
00:06:43,933 --> 00:06:47,257
He's probably in Chiba by now.

129
00:06:47,257 --> 00:06:48,469
What? Chiba?

130
00:06:48,469 --> 00:06:50,865
Whoa, whoa! Hold on!

131
00:06:50,865 --> 00:06:52,073
If she's not here, then it's fine.

132
00:06:52,073 --> 00:06:54,053
Anyway, this is good.
I'll head back to Tokyo too.

133
00:06:54,053 --> 00:06:58,061
Look, it wasn't a coincidence
that you missed each other.

134
00:06:58,061 --> 00:07:01,621
- What?
- Sakiko heard you were coming here.

135
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:03,677
So she went back to Tokyo.

136
00:07:03,677 --> 00:07:05,705
What?

137
00:07:05,705 --> 00:07:07,397
Take it easy.

138
00:07:07,397 --> 00:07:10,417
Forcing a meeting with
a woman who doesn't want to see you

139
00:07:10,417 --> 00:07:12,633
won't lead to a proper conversation.

140
00:07:13,677 --> 00:07:16,197
Let's have some watermelon.
Let's have some fish.

141
00:07:16,197 --> 00:07:20,253
Wait, what's your relationship
with Sacchan anyway?

142
00:07:21,317 --> 00:07:23,301
Ex-husband.

143
00:07:25,889 --> 00:07:29,153
Oh? You didn't know?

144
00:07:29,153 --> 00:07:31,933
I was married to Sakiko.

145
00:07:31,933 --> 00:07:33,273
What?

146
00:07:33,273 --> 00:07:36,341
My location got out through Chizuru.

147
00:07:36,341 --> 00:07:39,249
Then I heard that
Mitsuru was heading to Chiba.

148
00:07:39,249 --> 00:07:42,473
So I came back to Tokyo to avoid him.

149
00:07:42,473 --> 00:07:44,337
It was a deliberate miss.

150
00:07:44,337 --> 00:07:47,849
- What are you doing?
- Oh right, this is for you.

151
00:07:47,849 --> 00:07:49,169
Dried fish.

152
00:07:49,169 --> 00:07:52,110
Sorry, Sho might not be able to eat this.

153
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,857
Where's Sho?

154
00:07:53,857 --> 00:07:56,421
He's at the insect museum with my sister.

155
00:07:56,421 --> 00:07:59,865
I had something to do today,
so I couldn't take him.

156
00:07:59,865 --> 00:08:03,561
A meeting to uncover
the true nature of Sakiko Seo.

157
00:08:03,561 --> 00:08:05,797
What's that all about?

158
00:08:05,797 --> 00:08:07,842
No, seriously.

159
00:08:07,842 --> 00:08:09,787
Where have you been? What were you doing?

160
00:08:09,787 --> 00:08:14,661
I told you, we had a fight and I left home.

161
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:18,893
I stayed with a friend in Chiba
for a few days.

162
00:08:18,893 --> 00:08:20,021
That's all.

163
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:21,937
A friend?

164
00:08:21,937 --> 00:08:26,453
Mitsuru searched a lot
but couldn't find anything.

165
00:08:26,453 --> 00:08:28,333
My ex-husband.

166
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,493
You were divorced?

167
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:37,973
I see. Of course he wouldn't know
your ex-husband's contact info.

168
00:08:39,085 --> 00:08:41,773
He didn't know that I was married before.

169
00:08:42,845 --> 00:08:44,701
What?

170
00:08:45,705 --> 00:08:47,701
I never told him.

171
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:50,573
About my divorce history.

172
00:08:53,885 --> 00:08:55,557
Sakiko's husband?

173
00:08:55,557 --> 00:08:57,597
He's totally different from Daddy.

174
00:08:57,597 --> 00:09:00,117
What's wrong? Did you have a fight?

175
00:09:00,117 --> 00:09:02,169
Did she start hating you?

176
00:09:02,169 --> 00:09:05,245
Don't be mean. Come on, clean that up.

177
00:09:05,245 --> 00:09:06,461
Okay.

178
00:09:06,461 --> 00:09:07,937
Sorry.

179
00:09:07,937 --> 00:09:09,425
Well...

180
00:09:09,425 --> 00:09:14,029
Oh, that's Kokoa, my girlfriend.

181
00:09:14,029 --> 00:09:17,781
We're not married yet,
but I'm pretty much like a wife already.

182
00:09:17,781 --> 00:09:19,897
So?

183
00:09:19,897 --> 00:09:22,405
Oh, I'm not their biological mother.

184
00:09:22,405 --> 00:09:23,877
Wait! So...

185
00:09:23,877 --> 00:09:25,417
No, no, no.

186
00:09:25,417 --> 00:09:27,237
They're children I had with my second wife.

187
00:09:27,237 --> 00:09:30,293
The one I married after Sakiko.

188
00:09:30,293 --> 00:09:33,337
We're divorced,
but I let her see the kids once a month.

189
00:09:33,337 --> 00:09:34,661
We're on good terms.

190
00:09:34,661 --> 00:09:35,953
I bought it.

191
00:09:35,953 --> 00:09:37,821
Oh, Haru?

192
00:09:37,821 --> 00:09:39,297
- Here!
- Himeka!

193
00:09:39,297 --> 00:09:42,345
- Here!
- Okay! Cute, right?

194
00:09:42,345 --> 00:09:44,301
- That's enough. Here.
- Okay.

195
00:09:44,301 --> 00:09:46,117
Married and divorced twice?

196
00:09:46,117 --> 00:09:49,933
Only twice. I've still got a long way to go.

197
00:09:50,873 --> 00:09:53,105
By the way, Sakiko went back to Tokyo.

198
00:09:53,105 --> 00:09:56,193
Right, and this guy didn't know that.
He came here to pick her up.

199
00:09:56,193 --> 00:09:59,681
What? She ran away from you? That's pathetic.

200
00:09:59,681 --> 00:10:01,353
Pathetic.

201
00:10:01,353 --> 00:10:03,661
- Yeah, it's really pathetic, isn't it?
- So pathetic.

202
00:10:03,661 --> 00:10:04,781
I'm leaving.

203
00:10:04,781 --> 00:10:09,493
But you're the one
with the habit of running away, right?

204
00:10:10,913 --> 00:10:13,361
You disappeared for a whole year, didn't you?

205
00:10:13,361 --> 00:10:15,833
You left Sakiko all alone.

206
00:10:15,833 --> 00:10:18,589
And now you're just getting payback.

207
00:10:18,589 --> 00:10:21,177
Playing the victim?

208
00:10:21,177 --> 00:10:23,017
Who do you think you are?

209
00:10:26,345 --> 00:10:29,693
Well, whatever. I'm not saying
it's okay, but...

210
00:10:30,313 --> 00:10:34,493
But you must have had your reasons.

211
00:10:35,189 --> 00:10:38,289
All right, let's hear it over dinner.

212
00:10:38,289 --> 00:10:40,653
But first, let's drink.

213
00:10:40,653 --> 00:10:42,553
All right, have a seat.

214
00:10:45,161 --> 00:10:47,001
Here we go.

215
00:10:48,069 --> 00:10:51,289
Trying to force a meeting with a woman
who doesn't want to see you is pointless.

216
00:10:51,289 --> 00:10:53,613
It won't be a proper conversation.

217
00:10:54,353 --> 00:10:56,813
I just said that too!
I said the exact same thing.

218
00:10:56,813 --> 00:10:59,357
For real? We really click!

219
00:10:59,357 --> 00:11:01,605
- Wanna get married?
- As if!

220
00:11:01,605 --> 00:11:03,873
- Whatever.
- Shut up.

221
00:11:04,765 --> 00:11:06,873
All right.

222
00:11:06,873 --> 00:11:11,113
I reported to Chizuru, Naoto,
and Mr. Miyauchi that I'm home.

223
00:11:11,113 --> 00:11:12,665
Okay.

224
00:11:12,665 --> 00:11:16,713
Now please go home, for real.

225
00:11:18,377 --> 00:11:20,733
Mitsuru will be back.

226
00:11:22,757 --> 00:11:25,137
I just have to talk to him.

227
00:11:25,137 --> 00:11:28,633
Okay, I'll go home. Thanks for having me.

228
00:11:31,597 --> 00:11:33,185
Well, why?

229
00:11:33,185 --> 00:11:34,225
Huh?

230
00:11:34,225 --> 00:11:38,165
When you came back to Tokyo,
why did you come here first?

231
00:11:38,165 --> 00:11:40,493
Because I wanted to talk to you, Mr. Sonoda.

232
00:11:42,477 --> 00:11:47,445
You've been my outlet
for everything this past year.

233
00:11:47,445 --> 00:11:50,593
So when I wanted someone
who would listen to me,

234
00:11:50,593 --> 00:11:53,173
you were the first person I thought of.

235
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:57,509
Sorry for leaning on you.

236
00:11:57,509 --> 00:11:59,921
That's okay, but...

237
00:11:59,921 --> 00:12:03,725
No, I mean, it's fine,
and I'm happy that you did, but...

238
00:12:03,725 --> 00:12:05,381
Are you okay?

239
00:12:05,381 --> 00:12:07,081
Do you...

240
00:12:07,861 --> 00:12:10,413
Do you still love your husband?

241
00:12:15,529 --> 00:12:17,813
Wow, you're actually hesitating.

242
00:12:18,797 --> 00:12:24,149
Well, marriage isn't just about love, is it?

243
00:12:25,081 --> 00:12:27,693
It's a partnership.

244
00:12:28,317 --> 00:12:30,417
Ugh, that's so disappointing.

245
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:34,209
What, so you've become the kind of person
who says stuff like that too?

246
00:12:34,209 --> 00:12:37,957
You sounded stupid, always saying
"I love Mitsuru". That was way better.

247
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:39,257
- Stupid? Better?
- Anyway...

248
00:12:39,257 --> 00:12:41,713
What? We found out about
Mitsuru's disappearing habit.

249
00:12:41,713 --> 00:12:43,253
You hid your divorce history.

250
00:12:43,253 --> 00:12:45,077
You played tag between Tokyo and Chiba.

251
00:12:45,077 --> 00:12:46,861
And now you don't love him anymore?

252
00:12:46,861 --> 00:12:48,745
- You're heading straight for divorce.
- I didn't say that I don't love him.

253
00:12:48,745 --> 00:12:50,345
Don't talk about divorce so lightly.

254
00:12:50,345 --> 00:12:52,021
But you've already done it once.

255
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:54,173
Twice or three times, what's the difference?

256
00:12:58,405 --> 00:13:00,289
What? What is it?

257
00:13:00,289 --> 00:13:02,581
I'll call Mitsuru and apologize.

258
00:13:02,581 --> 00:13:05,089
I'll ask him to come home and we'll talk.

259
00:13:05,089 --> 00:13:10,005
Yeah, that's good. Do that.

260
00:13:12,597 --> 00:13:15,317
Oh, Mitsuru?

261
00:13:15,317 --> 00:13:17,501
I'm really sorry.

262
00:13:17,501 --> 00:13:19,877
I couldn't help it, running away like that.

263
00:13:20,825 --> 00:13:23,973
I want to talk to you properly,
so come back...

264
00:13:26,813 --> 00:13:28,637
Huh?

265
00:13:28,637 --> 00:13:31,133
Wait, you're at Atsuhiko's place?

266
00:13:32,433 --> 00:13:36,365
Mitsuru is staying at my ex-husband's place.

267
00:13:36,365 --> 00:13:39,493
- Well, then...
- What a unique couple.

268
00:13:39,493 --> 00:13:42,481
Ah, tell Atsuhiko that I said hi.

269
00:14:07,753 --> 00:14:09,837
Oh no, I don't have a key.

270
00:14:09,837 --> 00:14:11,637
Huh.

271
00:14:11,637 --> 00:14:14,485
So you've been together a long time, huh?

272
00:14:15,205 --> 00:14:20,705
Yeah, but still, there was
so much I didn't know.

273
00:14:22,341 --> 00:14:25,369
From your perspective,
what kind of person is Sacchan?

274
00:14:26,549 --> 00:14:29,249
What's the point of asking that?

275
00:14:29,249 --> 00:14:31,653
I want to know the real Sacchan.

276
00:14:33,305 --> 00:14:37,893
Is the Sakiko that someone else sees
the only true one?

277
00:14:39,665 --> 00:14:44,293
Is the Sakiko whom you're with a fake?

278
00:14:51,605 --> 00:14:54,533
Well, Micchan?

279
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:56,873
That's the first time
anyone's ever called me that.

280
00:14:56,873 --> 00:14:59,373
I'm sorry, I really am.

281
00:14:59,373 --> 00:15:02,013
- I'm sorry for everything.
- It's okay.

282
00:15:02,013 --> 00:15:04,553
I'm the one who let Mitsuru go there.

283
00:15:04,553 --> 00:15:06,933
Sorry for meddling.

284
00:15:06,933 --> 00:15:09,469
But I couldn't keep quiet anymore.

285
00:15:09,469 --> 00:15:11,993
You didn't do anything wrong, Chizuru.

286
00:15:11,993 --> 00:15:13,953
I can sleep on the floor or the couch...

287
00:15:13,953 --> 00:15:16,529
Then Chizuru and I will take the bed.

288
00:15:16,529 --> 00:15:18,145
And you can sleep on the couch, okay, Sakiko?

289
00:15:18,145 --> 00:15:19,529
- What?
- No way.

290
00:15:19,529 --> 00:15:21,593
We've broken up,
so we're not sleeping together.

291
00:15:21,593 --> 00:15:22,881
What?

292
00:15:22,881 --> 00:15:24,081
Huh?

293
00:15:24,081 --> 00:15:26,933
- Oh, is this your first time meeting?
- Yeah.

294
00:15:26,933 --> 00:15:29,141
My ex-boyfriend,
the one who's ten years younger.

295
00:15:29,141 --> 00:15:31,305
Hey, I'm the ex-boyfriend.

296
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,193
He just stopped by for a drink.

297
00:15:33,193 --> 00:15:34,949
It's fine, I'll send him home.

298
00:15:34,949 --> 00:15:36,397
Come on, let me stay over.

299
00:15:36,397 --> 00:15:38,837
You have your own key, right? Go home.

300
00:15:38,837 --> 00:15:41,273
- I do, but...
- Didn't you two break up?

301
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:43,285
Yes, we did.

302
00:15:43,285 --> 00:15:45,173
And he ended up getting divorced too.

303
00:15:45,173 --> 00:15:47,437
Listen, my wife cheated on me behind my back.

304
00:15:47,437 --> 00:15:51,673
They promised to be open about it,
but he couldn't forgive the sneaking around.

305
00:15:51,673 --> 00:15:53,233
What a unique couple.

306
00:15:53,233 --> 00:15:58,309
But somehow we're still friends.

307
00:15:58,309 --> 00:16:01,261
We get along, so it's easy.

308
00:16:01,261 --> 00:16:02,953
I see.

309
00:16:02,953 --> 00:16:05,413
You accept that so easily.

310
00:16:06,945 --> 00:16:09,937
I've been too quick to judge others.

311
00:16:09,937 --> 00:16:11,741
That's just how people are.

312
00:16:11,741 --> 00:16:14,233
In the end, we can only
live by our own values.

313
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:17,017
- Don't you say that. Go home already.
- All right, Sakiko, here you go.

314
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:19,253
- Let's drink together.
- Here, Sakiko, sit down, sit down.

315
00:16:19,253 --> 00:16:21,405
- It's more fun with three.
- Okay, just a little.

316
00:16:21,405 --> 00:16:23,173
Come on, hurry up.

317
00:16:40,509 --> 00:16:42,585
I'm home.

318
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:44,293
Welcome back.

319
00:16:52,817 --> 00:16:55,113
Welcome back.

320
00:16:55,113 --> 00:16:56,881
Yeah.

321
00:16:56,881 --> 00:16:58,649
I'm home.

322
00:17:02,461 --> 00:17:05,565
Sorry, let me tidy up. Hang on a sec.

323
00:17:05,565 --> 00:17:08,573
That's unusual. You're usually so tidy.

324
00:17:09,289 --> 00:17:11,329
Not really.

325
00:17:11,329 --> 00:17:13,853
I was just trying hard before.

326
00:17:14,861 --> 00:17:16,773
You were trying hard?

327
00:17:17,921 --> 00:17:19,645
Yeah.

328
00:17:31,405 --> 00:17:34,129
You heard about me
being married before, right?

329
00:17:34,129 --> 00:17:36,333
Yeah.

330
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:40,185
Sorry for hiding something so important.

331
00:17:40,185 --> 00:17:43,333
It's okay. I hid a lot too.

332
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:46,241
Being married once
in the past is no big deal.

333
00:17:46,241 --> 00:17:48,033
I was surprised, though.

334
00:17:50,013 --> 00:17:52,129
Have a seat.

335
00:17:52,129 --> 00:17:53,865
I want to explain things properly.

336
00:17:53,865 --> 00:17:55,593
Okay.

337
00:18:02,709 --> 00:18:05,209
Well...

338
00:18:06,697 --> 00:18:09,553
- Atsuhiko Hashizume.
- Yeah.

339
00:18:09,553 --> 00:18:12,597
I got married when I was 22.

340
00:18:12,597 --> 00:18:15,317
Back then, he was a high-flying stockbroker.

341
00:18:15,317 --> 00:18:18,073
But now he's a fisherman in Chiba.

342
00:18:18,073 --> 00:18:23,881
After the divorce, we'd occasionally
grab dinner when he came to Tokyo.

343
00:18:23,881 --> 00:18:27,373
This time was the first time
we'd met in about two years.

344
00:18:28,529 --> 00:18:31,573
I see. He seemed like a good guy.

345
00:18:31,573 --> 00:18:33,565
He treated me to some great food.

346
00:18:33,565 --> 00:18:37,009
And he listened to
a lot of my personal stories.

347
00:18:37,009 --> 00:18:41,501
I get it. I can also talk to him
about anything.

348
00:18:41,501 --> 00:18:43,493
He's the only one I'm still connected to.

349
00:18:43,493 --> 00:18:46,045
Yeah, that's totally fine.

350
00:18:46,045 --> 00:18:49,333
I only met up with Mrs. Sonoda once a month.

351
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:56,013
22, huh.

352
00:18:56,865 --> 00:18:59,265
You got married so young.

353
00:18:59,265 --> 00:19:01,041
Yeah.

354
00:19:05,733 --> 00:19:08,077
The second one was when I was 25.

355
00:19:08,077 --> 00:19:09,949
Huh?

356
00:19:09,949 --> 00:19:12,853
When you married me, you were like 31, right?

357
00:19:15,293 --> 00:19:17,657
What?

358
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,453
What?

359
00:19:26,381 --> 00:19:28,081
Found it.

360
00:19:36,705 --> 00:19:37,773
Your driver's license?

361
00:19:37,773 --> 00:19:40,009
[Sakiko Nakabayashi]

362
00:19:42,321 --> 00:19:43,529
[Sakiko Hashizume]

363
00:19:43,529 --> 00:19:45,789
This is from my first marriage.

364
00:19:45,789 --> 00:19:47,561
Your first marriage?

365
00:19:50,353 --> 00:19:51,635
[Sakiko Onizuka]
When I was 25, the second husband,

366
00:19:51,635 --> 00:19:53,261
a band member.

367
00:19:53,261 --> 00:19:56,233
I ended up with 'I'll support him' mentality.

368
00:19:56,233 --> 00:19:58,125
He never made it in music.

369
00:19:58,125 --> 00:20:00,817
No idea where he is or what he's doing now.

370
00:20:00,817 --> 00:20:02,793
He had a great voice.

371
00:20:04,945 --> 00:20:07,265
28, my third marriage.

372
00:20:07,265 --> 00:20:09,433
[Sakiko Baba]
A civil servant I met on Twitter.

373
00:20:09,433 --> 00:20:11,881
He worked at Hachioji City Hall.

374
00:20:11,881 --> 00:20:14,141
I thought I could finally settle down.

375
00:20:14,141 --> 00:20:17,145
But it was a record-breaking
three-month marriage.

376
00:20:17,145 --> 00:20:19,045
He had a lovely voice.

377
00:20:22,993 --> 00:20:26,293
Okay, so there were three.

378
00:20:27,069 --> 00:20:29,133
- No.
- Huh?

379
00:20:29,777 --> 00:20:31,257
One more.

380
00:20:31,257 --> 00:20:34,933
I didn't have a chance
to update it, so it's just here.

381
00:20:36,969 --> 00:20:38,793
Zennyoji...

382
00:20:38,793 --> 00:20:41,541
29, my fourth marriage.

383
00:20:41,541 --> 00:20:43,265
An entrepreneur.

384
00:20:44,261 --> 00:20:46,653
I was picked up at a late-night bar.

385
00:20:46,653 --> 00:20:49,725
The day after we registered our marriage,
his company went bankrupt.

386
00:20:50,377 --> 00:20:52,973
Apparently he's a YouTuber now.

387
00:20:54,729 --> 00:20:56,477
He had nice handwriting.

388
00:20:58,365 --> 00:21:02,329
I proposed to all four of them
and got married.

389
00:21:02,329 --> 00:21:05,693
And they all asked for a divorce.

390
00:21:06,721 --> 00:21:12,145
I think my expectations for
a husband and family were too high.

391
00:21:12,145 --> 00:21:15,241
And yet I kept repeating it.

392
00:21:16,033 --> 00:21:18,172
And then,

393
00:21:18,172 --> 00:21:21,437
the fifth one was when I was 31.

394
00:21:21,437 --> 00:21:23,629
Mitsuru Seo.

395
00:21:23,629 --> 00:21:25,977
Runs a coffee shop.

396
00:21:25,977 --> 00:21:28,773
We met at a friend's wedding.

397
00:21:29,657 --> 00:21:33,237
Kind, thoughtful.

398
00:21:33,237 --> 00:21:35,649
He cherishes me.

399
00:21:35,649 --> 00:21:37,949
I feel at ease with him.

400
00:21:39,593 --> 00:21:42,945
And he was the first to propose to me.

401
00:21:45,273 --> 00:21:48,569
When I renewed my license as Sakiko Seo...

402
00:21:48,569 --> 00:21:53,505
I was a little moved
when I saw that it still said Sakiko Seo.

403
00:21:53,505 --> 00:21:56,745
It was the first time
I'd kept the same last name for so long.

404
00:21:59,909 --> 00:22:02,385
Sorry. That's a lot, isn't it?

405
00:22:07,985 --> 00:22:09,893
I was surprised.

406
00:22:12,209 --> 00:22:14,013
Sorry for keeping quiet.

407
00:22:16,249 --> 00:22:18,121
The reason I couldn't tell you

408
00:22:18,813 --> 00:22:21,573
is the same as your disappearing habit.

409
00:22:23,969 --> 00:22:27,173
For the first time,
I didn't want to lose someone.

410
00:22:28,449 --> 00:22:32,329
I was scared that you'd hate me,
so I stayed silent.

411
00:22:33,721 --> 00:22:37,613
Why were you so obsessed with marriage?

412
00:22:39,877 --> 00:22:41,933
I wanted a family.

413
00:22:43,869 --> 00:22:46,661
I have plenty of friends.

414
00:22:46,661 --> 00:22:50,173
I get along with people at work, but...

415
00:22:50,913 --> 00:22:54,641
Even when I have fun hanging out or drinking,

416
00:22:54,641 --> 00:22:57,413
everyone goes home in the end, right?

417
00:22:58,341 --> 00:23:01,369
To a home with someone they want to be with.

418
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:04,241
I was jealous.

419
00:23:04,241 --> 00:23:06,005
That kind of...

420
00:23:06,729 --> 00:23:10,573
I wanted an ally in life,
so I searched for one.

421
00:23:12,269 --> 00:23:14,693
But four times, it didn't work out.

422
00:23:15,825 --> 00:23:19,165
So I thought, "That's it, it's impossible."

423
00:23:19,165 --> 00:23:24,481
But right when I was thinking that
my only family was my parents,

424
00:23:25,405 --> 00:23:27,293
I met you, Mitsuru.

425
00:23:29,277 --> 00:23:33,725
I was cautious, of course.
I mean, it was my fifth time.

426
00:23:33,725 --> 00:23:37,253
But you still married me.

427
00:23:38,865 --> 00:23:41,693
Yeah, I did.

428
00:23:43,669 --> 00:23:46,245
Unlike the others,

429
00:23:46,245 --> 00:23:49,493
it wasn't about wanting you
to become my family.

430
00:23:50,465 --> 00:23:53,229
I just wanted to make you happy.

431
00:23:53,993 --> 00:23:55,741
Me?

432
00:23:56,469 --> 00:23:58,193
Yes.

433
00:23:58,193 --> 00:24:02,601
I wanted to make you happy,

434
00:24:02,601 --> 00:24:05,353
not be made happy by you.

435
00:24:07,545 --> 00:24:11,141
I thought that with this feeling,
maybe it would be okay.

436
00:24:11,141 --> 00:24:16,001
And it really did last a long time.

437
00:24:16,853 --> 00:24:19,417
It became okay.

438
00:24:19,417 --> 00:24:24,177
Maybe it's like your disappearing habit.

439
00:24:24,177 --> 00:24:26,553
See?

440
00:24:26,553 --> 00:24:29,861
You said that being with me made things okay.

441
00:24:29,861 --> 00:24:31,625
Yeah.

442
00:24:32,497 --> 00:24:34,213
Yeah.

443
00:24:35,145 --> 00:24:36,869
Same.

444
00:24:39,229 --> 00:24:40,973
It's the same.

445
00:24:42,977 --> 00:24:46,173
Even the part where
it stopped working is the same.

446
00:24:48,549 --> 00:24:50,653
It hasn't stopped working.

447
00:24:51,729 --> 00:24:53,613
We're still married.

448
00:24:56,489 --> 00:24:58,277
Let's start over.

449
00:25:00,649 --> 00:25:02,141
What?

450
00:25:02,141 --> 00:25:03,969
Our life.

451
00:25:05,065 --> 00:25:06,413
Our life?

452
00:25:06,413 --> 00:25:09,605
I know I'm the last one to talk, but...

453
00:25:10,649 --> 00:25:14,557
I was lonely without you.

454
00:25:14,557 --> 00:25:16,373
I wanted you to come back.

455
00:25:17,825 --> 00:25:19,829
Yeah.

456
00:25:19,829 --> 00:25:21,505
You really are the last one to talk.

457
00:25:21,505 --> 00:25:24,817
I'm sorry. But thanks to this,
I understand now.

458
00:25:24,817 --> 00:25:26,885
I want to be with you from now on.

459
00:25:27,937 --> 00:25:29,729
Let's be together.

460
00:25:36,629 --> 00:25:38,401
What's wrong?

461
00:25:40,013 --> 00:25:42,153
Huh?

462
00:25:42,153 --> 00:25:43,829
Four times. You know that, right?

463
00:25:43,829 --> 00:25:45,741
You haven't said anything about that.

464
00:25:45,741 --> 00:25:47,701
You're the fifth. My fifth husband.
You know that, right?

465
00:25:47,701 --> 00:25:50,633
Well, you're probably the fifth person
I've dated, so it's the same.

466
00:25:50,633 --> 00:25:53,925
No, it's not the same.
It's totally different.

467
00:25:53,925 --> 00:25:57,441
I know I'm being a hypocrite,
but married and divorced four times,

468
00:25:57,441 --> 00:25:59,313
and hiding it all from the fifth husband.

469
00:25:59,313 --> 00:26:02,901
- That's messed up, even if it's me.
- I've disappeared over five times in total.

470
00:26:02,901 --> 00:26:04,469
- That's way more messed up than you.
- Well...

471
00:26:04,469 --> 00:26:06,729
Of course I also think
that's messed up, but...

472
00:26:06,729 --> 00:26:09,269
Geez...

473
00:26:19,129 --> 00:26:22,553
Isn't this fine?
Even if we're both messed up,

474
00:26:23,181 --> 00:26:25,265
as long as we just want to be together,

475
00:26:25,265 --> 00:26:27,261
and if that's clear, then that's enough.

476
00:26:31,097 --> 00:26:33,293
I see.

477
00:26:33,293 --> 00:26:35,053
Yeah.

478
00:26:39,725 --> 00:26:43,305
I was surprised about
your disappearing habit too.

479
00:26:43,305 --> 00:26:46,557
But it doesn't make me hate you.

480
00:26:46,557 --> 00:26:50,053
And even if I'd known earlier,
I still would have married you.

481
00:26:50,053 --> 00:26:52,653
Yeah, I feel the same way about you.

482
00:26:56,473 --> 00:27:00,909
Wanna try living a normal life again?

483
00:27:02,221 --> 00:27:03,929
Yeah.

484
00:27:07,497 --> 00:27:10,517
I get that wanting to run away
is unavoidable.

485
00:27:10,517 --> 00:27:13,161
Just tell me if you want to run away.

486
00:27:13,161 --> 00:27:16,581
Just say that you're going out,
even if you don't know when you'll be back.

487
00:27:16,581 --> 00:27:18,265
Got it.

488
00:27:18,265 --> 00:27:20,325
Well, then...

489
00:27:20,325 --> 00:27:24,605
- If I ever want a divorce, I'll let you know.
- That figures.

490
00:27:24,605 --> 00:27:26,361
That might be scary.

491
00:27:26,361 --> 00:27:29,533
Don't worry. I've always been
the one to get dumped.

492
00:27:29,533 --> 00:27:32,777
I won't be the one to leave so easily.

493
00:27:33,989 --> 00:27:38,469
Actually, not knowing when
you'll disappear again is pretty scary too.

494
00:27:38,469 --> 00:27:40,441
I see.

495
00:27:40,441 --> 00:27:42,341
I guess that makes us even, then.

496
00:27:45,421 --> 00:27:46,809
What should we do about dinner?

497
00:27:46,809 --> 00:27:47,905
Wanna go shopping?

498
00:27:47,905 --> 00:27:49,757
Yeah. The fridge is empty, right?

499
00:27:49,757 --> 00:27:52,281
Yeah. Okay, let's do the dishes first.

500
00:27:52,281 --> 00:27:53,853
If we do them together, it'll be quick.

501
00:27:53,853 --> 00:27:56,401
Okay, and then we'll go shopping
when we're done.

502
00:27:56,401 --> 00:27:58,261
- Let's go together.
- Okay.

503
00:28:01,733 --> 00:28:03,729
I think that even for things
we don't want to talk about...

504
00:28:03,729 --> 00:28:04,953
Yeah.

505
00:28:04,953 --> 00:28:10,033
we should still talk about the things
that both of us ought to know.

506
00:28:10,033 --> 00:28:12,945
- Let's try to listen.
- Yeah.

507
00:28:14,897 --> 00:28:18,253
Mr. Sonoda, his wife...

508
00:28:18,253 --> 00:28:21,325
I didn't ask her to come with me.

509
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,733
Yeah, I know.

510
00:28:25,733 --> 00:28:29,893
But I still think it was my fault.

511
00:28:29,893 --> 00:28:31,717
And I'll keep thinking that.

512
00:28:32,921 --> 00:28:34,909
Yeah.

513
00:28:34,909 --> 00:28:37,797
I'll try to think that
it's half my fault too.

514
00:28:37,797 --> 00:28:39,693
No, Sacchan...

515
00:28:39,693 --> 00:28:41,669
It's not unrelated.

516
00:28:41,669 --> 00:28:44,125
You're going to stay married to me, right?

517
00:28:44,125 --> 00:28:46,669
If you don't want to, I'll get a divorce.

518
00:28:46,669 --> 00:28:49,669
Wow, that's convincing coming from someone
who's done it four times.

519
00:28:49,669 --> 00:28:53,373
I can fill out the divorce papers in no time.

520
00:28:58,797 --> 00:29:02,353
- Mitsuru...
- Hm?

521
00:29:02,353 --> 00:29:05,421
Do you know about the 'loved one filter'?

522
00:29:05,421 --> 00:29:07,333
What's that?

523
00:29:07,333 --> 00:29:08,925
Never mind, it's nothing.

524
00:29:08,925 --> 00:29:09,997
What? What is it?

525
00:29:09,997 --> 00:29:12,617
- I'm curious. What is it?
- You don't need to know.

526
00:29:12,617 --> 00:29:15,053
"Loved one filter"?

527
00:29:15,965 --> 00:29:19,057
- Really, it's fine. Don't worry about it.
- Is it a filter that's put on you?

528
00:29:34,277 --> 00:29:36,085
Hey.

529
00:29:37,377 --> 00:29:39,213
Long time no see.

530
00:29:39,213 --> 00:29:41,265
Did something happen?

531
00:29:41,265 --> 00:29:42,885
- Hm?
- No.

532
00:29:42,885 --> 00:29:45,725
You looked like you wanted to talk,
so I came.

533
00:29:45,725 --> 00:29:48,449
I see. Thanks.

534
00:29:48,449 --> 00:29:51,189
Is it fun talking to Sacchan?

535
00:29:51,957 --> 00:29:53,981
Uh, well...

536
00:29:54,625 --> 00:29:56,821
More like easy.

537
00:29:56,821 --> 00:29:58,597
That.

538
00:29:59,257 --> 00:30:01,853
Like Mitsuru is for you, Azusa?

539
00:30:01,853 --> 00:30:03,685
That's it.

540
00:30:04,685 --> 00:30:06,665
I know.

541
00:30:06,665 --> 00:30:09,041
Should I have said something sooner?

542
00:30:09,041 --> 00:30:11,467
If I'd explained everything from the start,

543
00:30:11,467 --> 00:30:13,437
would you not have suspected an affair?

544
00:30:20,097 --> 00:30:22,765
You would have.

545
00:30:23,473 --> 00:30:26,181
You would have suspected anyway.

546
00:30:27,129 --> 00:30:30,469
You can't imagine it
unless it happens to you.

547
00:30:31,205 --> 00:30:34,869
That's just the limit of human imagination.

548
00:30:36,613 --> 00:30:39,849
But hiding things isn't the answer, either.

549
00:30:39,849 --> 00:30:42,477
Yeah, exactly.

550
00:30:45,733 --> 00:30:49,733
Marriage is hard, isn't it?

551
00:30:49,733 --> 00:30:51,785
Yeah.

552
00:31:06,793 --> 00:31:13,501
[Alarm snooze]

553
00:31:19,201 --> 00:31:20,965
Whoa, that startled me.

554
00:31:20,965 --> 00:31:22,809
Hm?

555
00:31:26,825 --> 00:31:29,573
You're next to me.

556
00:31:29,573 --> 00:31:31,461
I am.

557
00:31:31,461 --> 00:31:33,705
I was here when you went to sleep.

558
00:31:35,189 --> 00:31:38,069
Even though you were here,

559
00:31:38,069 --> 00:31:41,209
it felt like you'd be gone when I woke up.

560
00:31:41,821 --> 00:31:44,009
Like during this past year.

561
00:31:44,009 --> 00:31:46,377
Right.

562
00:31:51,837 --> 00:31:54,365
Don't 'right' me.

563
00:31:54,365 --> 00:31:56,117
Get up!

564
00:31:57,241 --> 00:31:59,053
Get up!

565
00:32:00,205 --> 00:32:02,869
Yeah, that's beautiful.

566
00:32:02,869 --> 00:32:05,817
- Okay.
- Let's try changing the background a bit.

567
00:32:05,817 --> 00:32:07,297
Okay.

568
00:32:07,297 --> 00:32:08,997
- I'll adjust it.
- Okay.

569
00:32:08,997 --> 00:32:10,213
Okay.

570
00:32:10,213 --> 00:32:11,385
Well?

571
00:32:11,385 --> 00:32:13,133
It's lovely. I think it's good.

572
00:32:13,133 --> 00:32:14,645
That's not what I meant.

573
00:32:14,645 --> 00:32:16,517
You told him everything, right?

574
00:32:19,213 --> 00:32:23,225
He wasn't as shaken as I thought he'd be.

575
00:32:23,929 --> 00:32:26,701
Divorce is nothing these days.

576
00:32:26,701 --> 00:32:29,625
Compared to a disappearing habit,
it's totally normal.

577
00:32:29,625 --> 00:32:33,337
Divorcing four times
comes pretty close, though.

578
00:32:34,377 --> 00:32:36,949
So nothing's changed.

579
00:32:36,949 --> 00:32:39,829
We're slowly getting back to our old life.

580
00:32:39,829 --> 00:32:41,561
And our feelings too.

581
00:32:42,425 --> 00:32:44,413
I guess I still love him.

582
00:32:44,413 --> 00:32:47,461
Oh, really? That's good, then.

583
00:32:47,461 --> 00:32:50,029
Okay, let's take the photo.

584
00:32:50,029 --> 00:32:53,233
Why don't you do a wedding photo?

585
00:32:53,233 --> 00:32:55,765
Actually, I've always wanted to.

586
00:32:55,765 --> 00:32:57,765
Sounds good.

587
00:32:57,765 --> 00:32:59,273
Try on some dresses before you go.
We have quite a few.

588
00:32:59,273 --> 00:33:03,253
Chizuru, we're working. Come on.

589
00:33:03,253 --> 00:33:06,329
- Thank you very much.
- What should we do about dinner?

590
00:33:11,157 --> 00:33:14,497
I wonder if Sakiko ever gets bored.

591
00:33:14,497 --> 00:33:16,437
She eats happily.

592
00:33:18,461 --> 00:33:23,449
Well, I guess if you're
enjoying life together again, that's good.

593
00:33:23,449 --> 00:33:25,185
Enjoying...

594
00:33:26,369 --> 00:33:30,273
Yeah, I'm trying. And Sacchan too.

595
00:33:33,329 --> 00:33:35,433
I'm home.

596
00:33:38,481 --> 00:33:40,513
Mitsuru?

597
00:33:46,593 --> 00:33:51,057
[Running late?]

598
00:34:23,413 --> 00:34:25,505
I'm home.

599
00:34:29,165 --> 00:34:31,973
Hm? What's wrong?

600
00:34:31,973 --> 00:34:34,125
You didn't reply to my messages.

601
00:34:34,125 --> 00:34:37,293
I just saw your message on LINE,
but I was already almost home.

602
00:34:37,293 --> 00:34:39,113
Sorry, I should have replied right away.

603
00:34:39,113 --> 00:34:41,281
What were you doing until this late?

604
00:34:41,281 --> 00:34:43,385
Huh? Working.

605
00:34:43,385 --> 00:34:46,381
Since I came back, I extended the hours.

606
00:34:47,281 --> 00:34:50,101
Oh, I heard.

607
00:34:50,101 --> 00:34:51,281
Right.

608
00:34:51,281 --> 00:34:54,449
Sorry, I don't check
my phone much during work.

609
00:34:54,449 --> 00:34:56,225
Sorry.

610
00:34:56,225 --> 00:34:58,133
I'll go heat up dinner.

611
00:35:12,373 --> 00:35:16,001
- Morning.
- Oh, morning.

612
00:35:16,001 --> 00:35:17,641
Breakfast is ready.

613
00:35:17,641 --> 00:35:19,261
Sorry.

614
00:35:19,261 --> 00:35:22,457
Huh? Did we run out of peanut butter?

615
00:35:22,457 --> 00:35:24,305
No.

616
00:35:24,305 --> 00:35:27,101
I just thought it'd be better
if you didn't get bored.

617
00:35:27,101 --> 00:35:30,205
We eat breakfast together a lot, so...

618
00:35:30,205 --> 00:35:32,693
Mm. Thanks.

619
00:35:34,493 --> 00:35:37,485
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

620
00:35:38,725 --> 00:35:41,885
I'm totally fine, you know.

621
00:35:41,885 --> 00:35:47,149
If you want to eat out,
or just go on a solo trip,

622
00:35:48,117 --> 00:35:50,829
feel free to do that.

623
00:35:51,457 --> 00:35:53,885
Mm, thanks.

624
00:35:57,737 --> 00:35:59,501
Tasty.

625
00:35:59,501 --> 00:36:01,489
Good.

626
00:36:09,465 --> 00:36:11,105
Excuse me, Mrs. Seo.

627
00:36:11,105 --> 00:36:12,981
Sorry.

628
00:36:13,965 --> 00:36:15,309
What's up, Mitsuru?

629
00:36:15,309 --> 00:36:18,565
<i>I forgot to mention this morning,
I'll be at the shop until closing today.</i>

630
00:36:18,565 --> 00:36:20,065
<i>I should be home around 9:30.</i>

631
00:36:20,065 --> 00:36:22,865
<i>If it's any later, I'll let you know.</i>

632
00:36:22,865 --> 00:36:24,549
<i>I'll have dinner at home.</i>

633
00:36:24,549 --> 00:36:27,981
Oh, okay. Got it, thanks.

634
00:36:27,981 --> 00:36:31,677
<i>Yeah. Good luck at work.</i>

635
00:36:31,677 --> 00:36:32,741
Okay.

636
00:36:32,741 --> 00:36:34,009
<i>Bye.</i>

637
00:36:34,009 --> 00:36:35,761
Bye.

638
00:36:43,097 --> 00:36:45,557
That used to happen all the time.

639
00:36:45,557 --> 00:36:49,021
He can't check my phone at work,
and our home is close by.

640
00:36:49,021 --> 00:36:52,753
He'd get home and be like,
"Oh, sorry, I just saw your message."

641
00:36:53,429 --> 00:36:55,425
Right, right.

642
00:36:55,425 --> 00:36:59,301
But now I get really anxious.

643
00:36:59,301 --> 00:37:01,449
Maybe he picked up on that.

644
00:37:01,449 --> 00:37:05,713
Mitsuru is being weirdly careful
not to make me anxious.

645
00:37:05,713 --> 00:37:06,885
What is this?

646
00:37:06,885 --> 00:37:10,737
Well, your husband is probably anxious too.

647
00:37:10,737 --> 00:37:13,645
He asked for details about my exes.

648
00:37:13,645 --> 00:37:15,093
Details?

649
00:37:15,093 --> 00:37:19,649
He said, "I think it'll help me and you
stay together, Sacchan."

650
00:37:19,649 --> 00:37:22,741
He asked me to tell him how I ended up
getting divorced previously.

651
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:26,061
Well, you've been divorced four times, right?
You've got a history.

652
00:37:26,061 --> 00:37:28,577
If I explain everything,

653
00:37:28,577 --> 00:37:32,133
it'll sharpen his kindness
and consideration even more.

654
00:37:32,133 --> 00:37:35,981
Though it feels like I'm making him
do that, and so I feel guilty.

655
00:37:35,981 --> 00:37:39,225
Well, things can't stay
exactly the same, can they?

656
00:37:39,225 --> 00:37:42,949
Since your histories have been
exposed to each other.

657
00:37:44,601 --> 00:37:47,105
That's not like you.

658
00:37:47,105 --> 00:37:51,801
Could you at least argue back?
Like, "please don't call it a 'history.'"

659
00:37:55,077 --> 00:37:59,693
Well, did you tell him that
you'd be here today?

660
00:37:59,693 --> 00:38:01,349
Yes.

661
00:38:01,349 --> 00:38:04,381
I said that since it's Saturday,
you would probably be here.

662
00:38:04,381 --> 00:38:08,389
I let him know that we'd be talking,
just the two of us.

663
00:38:08,389 --> 00:38:11,005
You're being incredibly
thoughtful, aren't you?

664
00:38:14,425 --> 00:38:17,493
Is it fun being together like that?

665
00:38:20,209 --> 00:38:25,489
He's important to me,
and I want him to be happy.

666
00:38:25,489 --> 00:38:28,381
- I love him.
- Ah, so you admit that you love him.

667
00:38:28,381 --> 00:38:31,897
You've still got
the 'loved one filter' on, huh?

668
00:38:31,897 --> 00:38:34,889
- But...
- Huh? What?

669
00:38:35,857 --> 00:38:38,461
If we're talking about fun,

670
00:38:38,461 --> 00:38:41,177
I have more fun with you, Mr. Sonoda.

671
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:44,509
- Well, thanks for that.
- No,

672
00:38:44,509 --> 00:38:46,949
maybe "fun" isn't exactly the right word.

673
00:38:46,949 --> 00:38:49,213
- Maybe it's just easier.
- No, it's fine if it's fun.

674
00:38:49,213 --> 00:38:51,081
"Fun" and "easy" do use
the same kanji, after all.

675
00:38:51,081 --> 00:38:53,609
- Look.
- Huh? What is it?

676
00:38:53,609 --> 00:38:56,557
- I'm practically bare-faced here.
- Come on, put some effort into it.

677
00:39:01,689 --> 00:39:04,317
Oh, right. Here, this is for Sho.

678
00:39:04,317 --> 00:39:06,001
It's a financier from Mitsuru's place.

679
00:39:06,001 --> 00:39:07,445
Oh, is it okay to give it away?

680
00:39:07,445 --> 00:39:10,453
Yes, he brings them home every day.

681
00:39:10,453 --> 00:39:12,373
Every day?

682
00:39:14,317 --> 00:39:17,113
It used to be just occasionally.

683
00:39:17,113 --> 00:39:20,561
I used to be happy when he brought them home.

684
00:39:39,481 --> 00:39:41,117
Hey.

685
00:39:41,117 --> 00:39:43,581
<i>Oh, you sound like you're doing well.</i>

686
00:39:43,581 --> 00:39:44,693
Then, bye.

687
00:39:44,693 --> 00:39:46,048
<i>Whoa, wait, wait.</i>

688
00:39:46,048 --> 00:39:48,989
<i>Don't just call me
and then hang up right away.</i>

689
00:39:49,817 --> 00:39:52,793
Well, I didn't have anything to say.

690
00:39:54,313 --> 00:39:56,269
Are you okay?

691
00:39:56,269 --> 00:40:00,209
Yeah, I'm just living with
my husband, as usual.

692
00:40:00,209 --> 00:40:03,149
<i>Oh, good, good.</i>

693
00:40:03,801 --> 00:40:06,565
<i>I heard a lot from that guy, you know.</i>

694
00:40:07,173 --> 00:40:11,321
I'm sure he really cares about you.

695
00:40:11,989 --> 00:40:13,777
<i>It's okay.</i>

696
00:40:14,421 --> 00:40:16,281
What about you?

697
00:40:16,281 --> 00:40:19,637
Is your life with Kokoa and the kids fun?

698
00:40:19,637 --> 00:40:21,957
<i>Yeah, it is.</i>

699
00:40:21,957 --> 00:40:26,185
<i>All my decisions are based on
whether it's fun or not.</i>

700
00:40:26,185 --> 00:40:28,229
Of course.

701
00:40:28,229 --> 00:40:29,953
What's wrong?

702
00:40:30,813 --> 00:40:35,753
We say "thank you" more than before.

703
00:40:36,557 --> 00:40:38,401
To each other.

704
00:40:38,401 --> 00:40:42,233
<i>Huh? That's a really good thing, isn't it?</i>

705
00:40:43,465 --> 00:40:45,641
Life, you know...

706
00:40:46,253 --> 00:40:48,973
Is it really supposed to be this much effort?

707
00:40:51,581 --> 00:40:53,301
Sacchan.

708
00:40:54,885 --> 00:40:56,589
I'm home. Are you on the phone?

709
00:40:56,589 --> 00:40:59,001
Yeah, it's fine.

710
00:40:59,001 --> 00:41:00,837
Here.

711
00:41:02,061 --> 00:41:03,809
Thanks.

712
00:41:09,933 --> 00:41:11,757
Are things really okay?

713
00:41:11,757 --> 00:41:14,105
Hey, you didn't cook the rice again.

714
00:41:14,105 --> 00:41:16,393
We promised we'd take turns.

715
00:41:16,393 --> 00:41:17,493
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

716
00:41:17,493 --> 00:41:20,169
How many times are you going to
repeat the same thing?

717
00:41:20,169 --> 00:41:23,377
How can you fillet a fish
but not cook rice in a rice cooker?

718
00:41:23,377 --> 00:41:26,153
We're having curry tonight.
You okay without rice?

719
00:41:26,153 --> 00:41:28,725
Sorry, I'm sorry. I'll do it right now.

720
00:41:28,725 --> 00:41:30,853
- Shut up.
- Huh? Did you say something?

721
00:41:30,853 --> 00:41:33,313
I didn't say anything.

722
00:41:40,473 --> 00:41:43,313
Should I use quick cook? Or regular?

723
00:41:43,313 --> 00:41:45,109
Regular's fine.

724
00:41:45,109 --> 00:41:46,845
Okay.

725
00:41:46,845 --> 00:41:48,693
Thanks.

726
00:41:51,917 --> 00:41:53,357
Anything else I should do?

727
00:41:53,357 --> 00:41:56,489
Oh, no, it's fine.
I'll do it, so just have a seat.

728
00:41:56,489 --> 00:41:59,377
The dryer's almost done,
so I'll fold the laundry after.

729
00:41:59,377 --> 00:42:00,469
Please.

730
00:42:00,469 --> 00:42:02,781
Oh, and I'll clean the bath while I'm at it.

731
00:42:02,781 --> 00:42:04,941
So we can hop in right after dinner.

732
00:42:04,941 --> 00:42:06,737
Thanks.

733
00:42:17,553 --> 00:42:19,729
What's that sound?

734
00:42:41,773 --> 00:42:43,541
What's wrong?

735
00:42:46,857 --> 00:42:48,557
Ah.

736
00:42:49,445 --> 00:42:51,425
It ripped.

737
00:42:51,425 --> 00:42:53,453
I wonder if we can buy just the part?

738
00:42:53,453 --> 00:42:55,965
I'll contact the manufacturer or something.

739
00:42:55,965 --> 00:42:59,117
As for the laundry that was washed...

740
00:43:00,497 --> 00:43:03,185
It looks okay. I'll fold it.

741
00:43:06,669 --> 00:43:09,217
- Thanks.
- No problem.

742
00:43:11,985 --> 00:43:14,057
Thanks for everything up to now.

743
00:43:22,889 --> 00:43:24,921
Let's get a divorce.

744
00:43:30,061 --> 00:43:32,217
<i>The filter ripped.</i>
